          "PlanSteelWeightLb": "NaN",
          "Unresolved": [
            "UNRESOLVED (p.148, p.254, p.259): pier 13 working point coordinates - the N / E printed for pier 13 on Bridge N (p.148, Ramp 44E STA 301\u002B09.58) lie about 171 ft from the pier 14 working point, not 139.28 ft along an R 881.47 arc, and Bridge O\u0027s staking sheet (p.259) gives no pier-13 coordinates. Pier 13 is located by station (301\u002B53.72 Ramp 44F) on the arc through piers 14 / 16; the p.148 coordinates are reported only.",
            "UNRESOLVED (p.254, p.270): superelevation transition - the deck sections show 6 % only; no superelevation diagram is in the volume. 6 % used over the whole unit.",
            "UNRESOLVED (p.273): pier 13 angles 69 deg 02\u002738\u0022 (G1) / 69 deg 18\u002754\u0022 (G2) - a straight bearing line crossing the concentric girders 18\u0027-11 13/16 apart meets them about 27\u0027 apart in angle, the plan angles differ by 16\u0027; with the elevation-sheet spans the angles come out about 44\u0027 (G1) and 33\u0027 (G2) smaller. The line is set by the girder spans 141\u0027-4\u0022 / 137\u0027-2 5/16\u0022 (which also give the plan\u0027s 18\u0027-11 13/16\u0022 along CL brg and CL pier at 301\u002B53.72); angles reported.",
            "UNRESOLVED (p.273): deck ends at piers 13 and 16 - the unit\u0027s slab continues into Bridge N (pier 13) and span 17 (pier 16); the joint / continuity details there are outside this unit. The modeled deck stops 1\u0022 short of CL pier 13 / CL pier 16 (DeckEndOffset 11\u0022 from CL brg): the 2\u0022 joint opening of p.271 note 1 at the CL pier; the joint device itself is not modeled.",
            "UNRESOLVED (p.270): F-shaped parapet FSHP-42 section (top width, face breaks) - the standard drawing FSHP-42 is not in the volume. Program F-shape with 42\u0022 height and 1\u0027-6 base; other dimensions = program defaults.",
            "UNRESOLVED (p.254-297): structural steel plan quantity - no estimate of quantities / steel weight for the tub unit was found in the volume. Steel weight is reported without a plan comparison.",
            "UNRESOLVED (p.278-279): thickness transitions at shop splices - the girder elevations show square steps; no taper detail is given. Plates change square at the dimensioned points (no 1:2.5 taper modeled).",
            "UNRESOLVED (p.281): web splice plate position on the web - the section dimensions 6 1/2\u0022 \u002B 3\u0027-6 1/2\u0022 \u002B 6 1/2\u0022 (4\u0027-7 1/2\u0022) exceed the 4\u0027-3 9/16\u0022 web length on the slope. Web splice plates centred on the web.",
            "UNRESOLVED (p.281): bottom splice plate edge dimension 8 3/4\u0022 - (77\u0022 - 63 1/2\u0022) / 2 = 6 3/4\u0022, not 8 3/4\u0022. Plates centred on the tub CL.",
            "UNRESOLVED (p.273): which panel points carry internal cross frames - the framing plan distinguishes solid / dashed lines graphically only. Even panel points (solid lines) = K frame \u002B top strut, odd = top strut, as drawn.",
            "UNRESOLVED (p.289): lateral WT flange level against the girder top flange - Detail A is a plan view only; no section shows the WT flange against the top flange. WT flange modeled directly under the girder top flange (bolted to it, no gusset - none is drawn).",
            "UNRESOLVED (p.292): anchor bolt rows at the end piers 13 / 16 - the expansion-pier plan (G1) shows one row 9\u0022 from the CL brg; the row side at each end is not labeled. Row placed 9\u0022 from the CL brg on the span side.",
            "UNRESOLVED (p.292): anchor bolt projection above the bottom flange and the embedment - the section gives 7\u0022 MIN. projection and 1\u0027-3\u0022 MIN. into the concrete, the bolt 3\u0027-0\u0022 overall. Top at the 7\u0022 minimum above the top of the bottom flange (the 3\u0027-0\u0022 bolt then sits about 1\u0027-8\u0022 into the concrete, more than the 1\u0027-3\u0022 minimum).",
            "UNRESOLVED (p.273): access hatch position reference - 4\u0027-3\u0022 is dimensioned from the CL hatch to the CL brg line drawn at the girder; the side (span) is from the drawing. Hatches 4\u0027-3\u0022 into spans 14 and 16 on the tub CL.",
            "UNRESOLVED (p.278-279): first stud at pier 13 - the row label reads \u0022STUD SPA ~ 1\u0027-0\u0022\u0022 with an unreadable leader. First stud row 1\u0027-0 from the CL brg (gives 9.97\u0022 / 7.96\u0022 spacing, within the 10\u0022 / 8\u0022 max).",
            "UNRESOLVED (p.279): G2 top tension zone over pier 14 - it is dimensioned 39\u0027-2 7/8\u0022 but FS1 \u002B 18\u0027-3 1/2\u0022 to FS2 - 19\u0027-0 5/8\u0022 is 41\u0027-8 3/4\u0022 (79\u0027-0 7/8\u0022 between the splices). Zone taken between the two BOTH zones (41\u0027-8 3/4\u0022)."
          ]
        }
